// __nUlakam/atippatY/kaNiqam.qmz — கணிதம் (math) helpers__
// கணிதத்திற்கான துணைச் செயல்கள்
//
// __Rounding, floor and ceiling come from the host because they need the__
// __decimal representation itself. What was built from those is split__
// __across the three files imported below.__

// __Split into the files below. This one keeps the name so that every__
// __`இறக்கு` of it still reaches every function it used to.__

இறக்கு "eNkaL.qmz";
இறக்கு "qokuppu.qmz";
இறக்கு "vikiqam.qmz";

// __வர்க்கமூலம்(மதிப்பு) is a host builtin now.__
//
// __It was Newton's method here, written in eTamil because the host had no__
// __square root and the arithmetic to build one was all the language gave.__
// __Forty iterations per call, and it was never quite exact: √25 came back__
// __as 5.000000000000000000000288615.__
//
// __The host computes it on the Decimal itself, not through f64, so it is__
// __both faster and exact — √25 is 5. A negative input is still a தவறு for__
// __the reason it always was: the root of a negative variance is a sign__
// __error upstream, and answering zero hides it inside a confidence figure__
// __that looks perfectly reasonable.__
//
// __A function defined here would shadow the builtin, so it is gone rather__
// __than delegating.__
